==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|knacken}}, related to {{cog|gml|knaken}}, {{m|gml|knakken}}, {{m|gml|knacken}}, {{cog|nds-de|knacken}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|de|De-knacken.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-weak|knackt|knackte|geknackt}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to make a cracking sound
#: {{uxi|de|Die Wurst '''knackte''' beim Reinbeissen.|The sausage made a cracking sound when bitten.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[crack]] (open)
#: {{ux|de|Er '''knackte''' die Nuss.|He '''cracked''' the nut.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|figuratively}} to crack (a mystery, secret, etc.); to [[persuade]] (to reveal something)
#: {{ux|de|Sie '''knackte''' den Code.|She '''cracked''' the code.}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich kann ihn '''knacken'''.|I can get him to open up.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[pick]] (a lock)
# {{lb|de|intransitive|informal}} to sleep
#: ''Mach' nicht solchen Lärm, er '''knackt''' gerade.''

